  m_Name: 22 - Nested Loop
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_nested_loop
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Nested Loop
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'A loop can also be placed inside another loop. This is called a nested
    loop. Example:

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>for</color>
    i <color=#D96DD3>in</color> <color=#F5F5AB>range</color>(<color=#B5CEA8>3</color>):</font>

    <indent=3em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D96DD3>for</color> j <color=#D96DD3>in</color> <color=#F5F5AB>range</color>(<color=#B5CEA8>2</color>):</font>

    <indent=5em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#33CC66>move_forward</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font></indent>

    <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#33CC66>turn_right</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font></indent></indent>

    The
    inner loop fully executes every time the outer loop repeats.


    In this example:

    <indent=2em>-
    The outer loop repeats 3 times</indent>

    <indent=2em>- The inner loop repeats
    2 times during each outer repetition</indent>

    <indent=2em>- <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#33CC66>move_forward</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font> executes
    a total of 6 times</indent>

    <indent=2em>- <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#33CC66>turn_right</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font>
    executes a total of 3 times</indent>


    Nested loops can also combine different
    types of loops, such as placing a <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>while</color></font>
    loop inside a <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>for</color></font> loop,
    or vice versa.'
  isImageBig: 0
